\ Spitfire: the countryside near the aircraft. Each kilometre of land within
\ 3 km is divided by hedges into about sixteen fields, with trees along the
\ hedges and now and then a farm, a house and a barn about a yard; lanes run
\ straight through whole rows and columns of kilometres. The layout comes
\ from a hash of the kilometre's position, so the same fields are there
\ whenever the aircraft returns. A kilometre of water has ripples instead,
\ short strokes on the surface, more of them next to an aircraft below 400 m.
\ Kilometres within reach of a town or an airfield are left clear for their
\ own buildings. The objects of the kilometres near the aircraft are kept and
\ gathered again only when the aircraft crosses into another kilometre or
\ through 400 m.

3 constant countryside-reach

variable countryside-objects
{ } to countryside-objects
variable countryside-collection
{ :objects [ ] :centres 0 4 0-matrix :radii 0 1 0-matrix } to countryside-collection
variable countryside-cell
[ null null ] to countryside-cell

\ the places whose surroundings stay clear of fields, with how far
[ [ :edinburgh-castle 3500 ] [ :leith 1500 ] [ :glasgow-cathedral 4500 ] [ :govan 2000 ] [ :clydebank 1500 ]
  [ :inverness-castle 2000 ] [ :stirling-castle 1500 ] [ :turnhouse 1200 ] [ :drem 1200 ]
  [ :abbotsinch 1200 ] [ :dalcross 1200 ] [ :nidaros 2500 ] [ :vaernes 1200 ] ] to clear-places

\ whether a kilometre's centre lies within a clear place's reach
: clear-cell? ( x z -- flag )
	| x z |
	clear-places ( place |
		place first landmark-ground to centre
		centre first x - sq centre 2 @i z - sq + sqrt place second <
	) any? ;

0x8c8878 constant road-colour

\ a kilometre of water's ripples: strokes 60 m long running east and west, those that fall on water; null when none does
: ripples ( column row n-strokes -- object )
	| column row n-strokes |
	land-origin-x column land-cell * + to west
	land-origin-z row land-cell * + to south
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + to seed
	new-sketch to waves
	0 to n-drawn
	0 n-strokes 1 do k
		seed k 2.3 * + hash-fraction land-cell * west + to x
		seed k 4.7 * + 0.5 + hash-fraction land-cell * south + to z
		x z water-at? if
			waves [ [ x 30 - 0 z ] [ x 30 + 0 z ] ] sketch-path
			++ n-drawn
		then
	loop
	n-drawn 0 = if null exit then
	waves bank-colour sketch>object ;

\ a line along the ground at sea level, a point every 100 m, so it can follow the ground once lifted
: ground-line ( sketch from onto coastal -- )
	| sketch from onto coastal |
	onto from v- v-length 100 / round-up 1 max2 to n-pieces
	[ 0 n-pieces 1+ 1 do k from onto k n-pieces / v-between loop ] to points
	coastal not if sketch points sketch-path exit then
	[ ] to run
	0 points size 1+ 1 do k
		k points size < if points k @i to point point first point 2 @i water-at? not else false then if
			run point add-last! drop
		else
			run size 1 > if sketch run sketch-path then
			[ ] to run
		then
	loop ;

\ whether a kilometre touches the water: any of its corners, the middles of its sides or its centre on water
: coastal-cell? ( west south -- flag )
	| west south |
	[ 0 0.5 1 ] ( across | [ 0 0.5 1 ] ( along | west across land-cell * + south along land-cell * + water-at? ) map ) map flatten ( wet | wet ) any? ;

\ a sketch's points raised by the ground's height under them, from the hill cones given and the terrain
: lift-sketch ( sketch cones -- )
	| sketch cones |
	sketch sketch@points ( point | [ point first point second point first point 2 @i cones ground-height-under + point 2 @i ] ) map :points ! drop ;

\ the hill cones that may stand under a kilometre, and whether the kilometre needs lifting at all: a cone near it, or the Norwegian terrain's grid round it
: cell-cones ( west south -- cones lift )
	| west south |
	west land-cell 2 / + to centre-x
	south land-cell 2 / + to centre-z
	hill-cones ( cone | cone first centre-x - sq cone second centre-z - sq + sqrt cone 2 @i land-cell + < ) filter to near
	near
	near size 0 >
	centre-x terrain-west land-cell - > centre-x terrain-west terrain-columns terrain-spacing * + land-cell + < and
	centre-z terrain-south land-cell - > and centre-z terrain-south terrain-rows terrain-spacing * + land-cell + < and or ;

\ the lanes: a row or column of kilometres carries one straight through its middle when its hash says so, a fifth of them, so a lane runs on from one kilometre to the next
: lane-row? ( row -- flag ) 7.7 * 3.1 + hash-fraction 0.2 < ;
: lane-column? ( column -- flag ) 5.9 * 1.3 + hash-fraction 0.2 < ;

\ one kilometre's lanes, each two lines 6 m apart, as one object; null when it has none
: lanes ( column row west south coastal -- object )
	| column row west south coastal |
	new-sketch to roads
	false to any-lane
	row lane-row? if
		[ -3 3 ] ( side | roads [ west 0 south 500 + side + ] [ west land-cell + 0 south 500 + side + ] coastal ground-line ) each
		true to any-lane
	then
	column lane-column? if
		[ -3 3 ] ( side | roads [ west 500 + side + 0 south ] [ west 500 + side + 0 south land-cell + ] coastal ground-line ) each
		true to any-lane
	then
	any-lane not if null exit then
	roads@edges size 0 = if null exit then
	west south cell-cones to lift to cones
	lift if roads cones lift-sketch then
	roads road-colour sketch>object ;

\ one kilometre's objects: on land its hedges, three each way at jittered quarters, about sixteen fields; ten trees along the hedges; three times in ten a farm, a house and a barn about a yard; its lanes. On water its ripples, eighty when the eye is near and low, else twelve. In a town nothing
: cell-objects ( column row dense -- objects )
	| column row dense |
	land-origin-x column land-cell * + to west
	land-origin-z row land-cell * + to south
	west land-cell 2 / + south land-cell 2 / + water-at? if
		column row dense if 80 else 12 then ripples to waves
		waves null? if [ ] else [ waves ] then exit
	then
	west land-cell 2 / + south land-cell 2 / + clear-cell? if [ ] exit then
	column 7.31 * row 13.17 * + to seed
	west south coastal-cell? to coastal
	new-sketch to fields
	fields [ west 0 south ] [ west land-cell + 0 south ] coastal ground-line
	fields [ west 0 south ] [ west 0 south land-cell + ] coastal ground-line
	[ 1 2 3 ] ( quarter | seed quarter 1.7 * + hash-fraction 0.15 * quarter 0.25 * + 0.075 - land-cell * west + ) map to hedge-xs
	[ 1 2 3 ] ( quarter | seed quarter 2.9 * + 0.4 + hash-fraction 0.15 * quarter 0.25 * + 0.075 - land-cell * south + ) map to hedge-zs
	hedge-xs ( x | fields [ x 0 south ] [ x 0 south land-cell + ] coastal ground-line ) each
	hedge-zs ( z | fields [ west 0 z ] [ west land-cell + 0 z ] coastal ground-line ) each
	0 10 1 do k
		seed k 3.1 * + hash-fraction to t
		k 2 mod 0 = if
			[ hedge-xs k 3 mod @i 0 south t land-cell * + ]
		else
			[ west t land-cell * + 0 hedge-zs k 3 mod @i ]
		then
		to base
		coastal if base first base 2 @i water-at? else false then not if
			fields base seed k 5.3 * + hash-fraction 6 * 8 + sketch-tree
		then
	loop
	hedge-xs first 40 + to farm-x
	hedge-zs first 40 + to farm-z
	seed 4.2 + hash-fraction 0.3 < coastal if farm-x farm-z water-at? not else true then and if
		seed 90 * to farm-heading
		fields [ farm-x 0 farm-z ] farm-heading 10 16 6 9 sketch-house
		fields [ farm-x 0 farm-z ] farm-heading 25 0 0 placed farm-heading 12 24 7 10 sketch-house
		fields [ farm-x 0 farm-z ] farm-heading 12 0 22 placed farm-heading 30 20 0 rectangle-corners sketch-loop
	then
	west south cell-cones to lift to cones
	lift if fields cones lift-sketch then
	fields field-colour sketch>object to field-object
	column row west south coastal lanes to lane-object
	lane-object null? if [ field-object ] else [ field-object lane-object ] then ;

\ the kilometres near a point: their objects, built once each and kept; the kilometres next to the point's own, while the point is below 400 m, in their dense form; gathered again when the point crosses into another kilometre or through 400 m
: refresh-countryside ( position -- )
	| position ^countryside-collection ^countryside-cell |
	position first land-origin-x - land-cell / round-down to column
	position 2 @i land-origin-z - land-cell / round-down to row
	position second 400 < to low
	countryside-cell [ column row low ] = if exit then
	[ column row low ] to countryside-cell
	[ ] to near-objects
	column countryside-reach - column countryside-reach + 1 + 1 do c
		row countryside-reach - row countryside-reach + 1 + 1 do r
			low c column - abs 1 <= and r row - abs 1 <= and to dense
			c r dense if "{1}/{0}/dense" else "{1}/{0}" then format string>symbol to key
			countryside-objects key has? not if
				countryside-objects c r dense cell-objects key ! drop
			then
			near-objects countryside-objects key @ concat to near-objects
		loop
	loop
	near-objects collect-objects to countryside-collection ;
